@c -*-texinfo-*-
@c Per-crate manual: autoeq
@node autoeq Manual
@chapter Crate @code{autoeq}
@cindex autoeq
@cindex RoomEQ

@code{autoeq} is the offline optimisation engine that turns measurement
data into corrective filters for speakers, headphones and rooms. It
ships several binaries -- @code{autoeq}, @code{roomeq},
@code{convert-recording}, @code{autoeq-download-speakers} and a family
of QA harnesses -- plus a library used by the GPUI and TUI front-ends.

@menu
* autoeq User Guide::               Overview, capabilities, exports.
* autoeq Binary::                   Speaker / headphone CLI with examples.
* roomeq Binary::                   Room CLI with examples.
* How RoomEQ Works::                Pipeline, stages, algorithms.
* RoomEQ Config Schema::             Configuration JSON schema.
* RoomEQ DSP Chain Schema::            DSP chain JSON schema.
* autoeq Developer Guide::          Layout, public API, conventions.
@end menu

@node autoeq User Guide
@section User Guide

@subheading What it does

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Speaker EQ}: parametric IIR from CEA2034 / Spinorama
  measurements (anechoic).
@item @strong{Headphone EQ}: filters targeting Harman or custom
  curves.
@item @strong{Room EQ}: stereo through full home-cinema, multi-sub
  alignment, Double Bass Array (DBA), gradient cardioid pairs --
  IIR, FIR or hybrid output.
@end itemize

@subheading Optimisation back-ends

Optimiser names are looked up in @code{src/optim/registry.rs}. The
core back-ends:

@multitable @columnfractions .30 .50 .20
@headitem Backend @tab What it is @tab Best for
@item @code{autoeq:de} @tab Differential Evolution + JADE / L-SHADE
  variants @tab global, multimodal
@item @code{autoeq:cobyla} @tab Pure-Rust COBYLA @tab fast local
  refinement
@item @code{autoeq:isres} @tab Improved Stochastic Ranking ES @tab
  constrained global
@item @code{autoeq:cmaes} @tab CMA-ES @tab ill-conditioned problems
@item @code{autoeq:nsga2}, @code{autoeq:nsga3} @tab Pareto multi-
  objective @tab multi-curve fitting
@item @code{mh:pso}, @code{mh:firefly}, @dots{} @tab Metaheuristics
  bridge @tab experimentation
@end multitable

The historical @code{nlopt:*} names are compatibility aliases mapped
to pure-Rust back-ends with a warning. The NLopt C-FFI backend has
been removed.

@subheading Loss types

@table @code
@item speaker-flat
ERB-weighted MSE between corrected curve and target.
@item speaker-flat-asymmetric
Penalises boosts more than cuts.
@item speaker-score
Olive / Toole preference score (NBD + LFX + SM-PIR).
@item headphone-flat, headphone-score
Headphone variants.
@item drivers-flat
Multi-driver crossover fit.
@item multi-sub-flat
Multi-subwoofer combined-response fit.
@item epa
Zwicker/Fastl perceptual composite (flatness + sharpness + roughness
+ loudness balance + cubic-distortion-tone level + modal temporal
masking).
@end table

@subheading Export formats

JSON (canonical), Equalizer APO / Peace, CamillaDSP YAML,
EasyEffects preset, Wavelet GraphicEQ, PipeWire SPA-JSON, Roon DSP
preset, RME, AU Preset. Some targets (EasyEffects, Wavelet GraphicEQ)
do not support routing matrices or convolution; the exporter refuses
those configurations explicitly rather than silently dropping plugins.

