@node roomeq Binary
@section The @code{roomeq} Binary
@cindex roomeq binary

@code{roomeq} optimises a multi-channel speaker system from real-room
measurements and emits a per-channel DSP chain.

@example
roomeq --config <config.json> --output <output.json> [OPTIONS]
@end example

@subheading Key flags

@multitable @columnfractions .30 .15 .55
@headitem Flag @tab Default @tab What it does
@item @code{--config} @tab @i{required} @tab Room configuration JSON
  (see @ref{RoomEQ Config Schema}).
@item @code{--output} @tab @i{required} @tab Output DSP chain JSON
  (see @ref{RoomEQ DSP Chain Schema}).
@item @code{--sample-rate} @tab 48000 @tab Filter design rate (Hz).
@item @code{--verbose} @tab off @tab Verbose progress output.
@item @code{--help} @tab @tab Print help and exit.
@end multitable

All algorithmic choices (algorithm, filter count, bounds, loss,
features) live in the config file, not in CLI flags. This means the
exact run is reproducible from the config alone.

@subheading Examples

@strong{Stereo, single COBYLA pass.}

@example
roomeq \
  --config  measurements/stereo.json \
  --output  /tmp/stereo_dsp.json
@end example

Minimal @file{stereo.json}:

@example
@{
  "speakers": @{
    "left":  "measurements/left.csv",
    "right": "measurements/right.csv"
  @},
  "optimizer": @{
    "num_filters": 10,
    "algorithm": "nlopt:cobyla",
    "max_iter": 5000,
    "min_freq": 20.0,
    "max_freq": 20000.0,
    "min_q": 0.5, "max_q": 10.0,
    "min_db": -12.0, "max_db": 12.0,
    "loss_type": "flat"
  @}
@}
@end example

@strong{Stereo 2.1 with explicit topology and bass management.}

@example
@{
  "system": @{
    "model": "stereo",
    "speakers": @{ "L": "left_meas", "R": "right_meas",
                  "LFE": "sub_meas" @},
    "subwoofers": @{
      "config": "single",
      "crossover": "bass_xo",
      "sub_meas": "L"
    @}
  @},
  "crossovers": @{
    "bass_xo": @{ "type": "LR24", "frequency": 80.0 @}
  @},
  "speakers": @{
    "left_meas":  "measurements/L.csv",
    "right_meas": "measurements/R.csv",
    "sub_meas":   "measurements/sub.csv"
  @},
  "optimizer": @{ "num_filters": 8, "algorithm": "autoeq:de" @}
@}
@end example

@strong{Multi-subwoofer, modal-basis seat optimisation.}

@example
@{
  "speakers": @{
    "lfe": @{
      "name": "subs",
      "subwoofers": [
        @{ "measurements":
            ["sub1_seat0.csv","sub1_seat1.csv","sub1_seat2.csv"] @},
        @{ "measurements":
            ["sub2_seat0.csv","sub2_seat1.csv","sub2_seat2.csv"] @}
      ]
    @}
  @},
  "optimizer": @{
    "multi_seat": @{
      "enabled": true,
      "strategy": "modal_basis",
      "per_sub_peq": true,
      "global_eq": true,
      "allpass_filters_per_sub": 1
    @}
  @}
@}
@end example

@strong{Home cinema with group-aware crossover search.}

The same @code{system.model: "home_cinema"} block carries all front /
surround / surround-back / height / LFE channels. Roles are grouped
so a single crossover decision covers each group rather than fighting
across symmetric channels.

@subheading Targeted run from the test suite

@example
cargo run --release --bin roomeq -- \
  --config crates/autoeq/tests/data/roomeq/test_config_stereo.json \
  --output /tmp/out.json
@end example

@subheading QA harnesses

The crate also ships @code{roomeq-fuzzer},
@code{roomeq-qa-quality}, @code{roomeq-qa-coverage},
@code{roomeq-qa-features} and @code{roomeq-qa-synthetic}. Invoke
through @code{just qa-roomeq} for the convergence suite.

