@node How RoomEQ Works
@section How RoomEQ Works
@cindex roomeq pipeline

This section is a condensed version of
@file{crates/autoeq/docs/roomeq_explained.md}. Read that file for
the mermaid diagrams and the full equation set.

@subheading Big picture

A run is fully described by a single JSON configuration:

@table @code
@item speakers
Map from logical name to measurement source (CSV / WAV / API curve /
@code{Group} / @code{MultiSubGroup} / @code{DBA} / @code{Cardioid}
aggregate).
@item system
(Optional.) Explicit topology -- @code{Stereo}, @code{Stereo 2.1},
@code{HomeCinema}, @code{Custom}. When present, selects a specialised
workflow instead of the generic per-channel path.
@item crossovers
Named filter blocks used by multi-driver speakers and bass management
(@code{LR24}, @code{LR48}, @code{BW12}, @code{BW24}).
@item optimizer
Target curve, algorithm, filter count, Q / gain / freq bounds, and
feature toggles (Schroeder split, excursion protection, phase
alignment, multi-seat, CEA-2034 pre-correction, mixed-phase, @dots{}).
@end table

@subheading Pipeline stages

@code{optimize_room()} (entry point in @file{src/roomeq/optimize.rs})
dispatches into @code{RoomPipeline::run()}, which emits these stages:

@enumerate
@item @code{ConfigPreparation} -- clone config; if
  @code{cea2034_correction.enabled}, fetch Spinorama bundles into a
  cache used by the per-channel workflow.
@item @code{Validation} -- structural checks: every role points to a
  real speaker, every named crossover is defined, every measurement
  source loads and parses, phase data is present where required, and
  filter frequency bounds lie within the measurement support of every
  channel.
@item @code{TopologyRouteSelection} -- pick the workflow:
  @code{Stereo} / @code{Stereo 2.1} / @code{HomeCinema} or the generic
  per-channel path.
@item @code{TopologyWorkflowExecution} @i{or}
  @code{GenericChannelOptimization} -- the actual optimisation.
@item @code{FirGeneration} when @code{processing_mode} is
  @code{PhaseLinear} or @code{Hybrid}.
@item @code{MixedPhaseFirGeneration} when @code{MixedPhase}.
@item @code{PhaseCorrection} when configured (rePhase-style all-pass).
@item @code{GroupDelayOptimization} when configured.
@item @code{ImpulseResponseComputation} -- pre/post IR for plotting.
@item @code{ChannelMatching} (>= 2 channels) -- inter-channel
  deviation report + spectral alignment + ``voice of god'' timbre
  matching.
@item @code{MetadataRefresh} -- pre/post scores, EPA, bass-management
  report.
@item @code{SanityCheck} -- non-NaN, length-matched arrays;
  @code{debug_assert!} in debug, clean @code{Err} in release.
@end enumerate

@subheading Per-channel optimisation

Every channel -- whether reached from a topology workflow or the
generic path -- goes through @code{process_single_speaker}:

@enumerate
@item @strong{Load measurement} via @code{load_source}; resample onto
  the optimiser grid; 1/N-octave smooth.
@item @strong{Build target} (@code{target_tilt.rs}): base shape
  (@code{flat}, @code{harman}, @code{custom}, @code{file},
  @code{from_measurement}) plus user-preference bass / treble shelves.
@item @strong{Detect F3} and generate a highpass to keep the optimiser
  from boosting below the driver rolloff (excursion protection).
@item @strong{Phase alignment} (@code{phase_alignment.rs}): coarse
  0.5 ms / refined 0.1 ms grid over sub vs main delay and polarity.
@item @strong{Multi-seat / SFM} (@code{multiseat.rs}): per-sub PEQ,
  then MSO/SFM over the corrected matrix for per-sub gain, delay,
  polarity and optional all-pass. Strategies:
  @code{minimize_variance}, @code{primary_with_constraints},
  @code{average}, @code{modal_basis} (SVD over complex per-sub /
  per-seat transfer functions, picks dominant non-common modes).
@item @strong{EQ search} (@code{speaker_eq/schroeder.rs}): single-pass
  or Schroeder-split (modal band high-Q / statistical band low-Q),
  driven by the chosen optimiser back-end.
@item @strong{FIR post-generation} (@code{fir.rs}): for
  @code{PhaseLinear} / @code{Hybrid}, inverse-FFT the magnitude
  response; for @code{MixedPhase}, cepstral decomposition + excess-
  phase corrector.
@item @strong{Group-delay optimisation} (@code{gd_opt.rs}): emits
  delay / polarity / all-pass plugins, or folds delay into the FIR
  shift in @code{PhaseLinear} mode.
@item @strong{Build chain} (@code{output.rs}): assemble the per-
  channel plugin list in order
  @code{gain -> delay -> eq -> convolution -> @dots{}}.
@end enumerate

@subheading Optional advanced corrections

@table @asis
@item Decomposed correction (Laborie/Bruno/Montoya, 2003)
Split the IR into modal, early-reflection and steady-state regions
and apply different strategies to each.
@item First-reflection cancellation (Johnston, AES 2008)
Subtract a delayed low-passed copy below ~500 Hz.
@item Spatial robustness (Brännmark / Sternad, AES 2008)
Trade single-point flatness for cross-position robustness with a
spatial zero-clustering pre-ringing constraint.
@item Mixed-phase / phase correction
Short FIR that corrects excess phase without doubling latency.
@end table

@subheading Schroeder split

The Schroeder frequency separates modal (sparse high-Q resonances)
from statistical (overlapping modes) room behaviour. Estimated by
@code{estimate_schroeder_frequency} as
@code{2000 * sqrt(T_60 / V)} or, when only volume is known, by
@code{11885 / sqrt(V)}. When @code{schroeder_split.enabled = true}
the optimiser runs two passes:

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Low band} (@code{min_freq} -- @code{f_S}): high Q, no
  boost.
@item @strong{High band} (@code{f_S} -- @code{max_freq}): low Q,
  optionally shelves only.
@end itemize

The biquad sets are concatenated.

@subheading Output

@code{DspChainOutput} carries per-channel @code{plugins} arrays,
@code{global_plugins} (sparse matrix for bass-management routing),
and a metadata block with pre/post scores, EPA per channel, optimiser
algorithm, iteration counts, version stamp, and a full
@code{BassManagementReport}.

@subheading References

The roomeq pipeline cites: CTA-2034-A (spinorama), Olive preference
score (AES 2004), Harman in-room target (Olive/Welti/McMullin),
Schroeder (JASA 1962/1996), Brännmark & Sternad (AES 2008 +
EP2104374B1), Laborie/Bruno/Montoya (AES 2003), Johnston (AES 2008),
Glasberg/Moore ERB, Zwicker/Fastl psychoacoustics, ISO 226,
DIN 45692, Sobol sequences, NSGA-II, Welti/Devantier multi-sub
optimisation. Full bibliography: @file{crates/autoeq/REFERENCES.md};
optimisation algorithms:
@file{crates/math-audio/math-optimisation/REFERENCES.md}; filters:
@file{crates/math-audio/math-iir-fir/REFERENCES.md}.

