@node RoomEQ Config Schema
@section RoomEQ Input Format
@cindex roomeq input format

The complete schema lives in
@file{crates/autoeq/bin/roomeq/input_schema.json} and is documented in
@file{INPUT_FORMAT.md}. Validate a config with:

@example
npx ajv validate -s input_schema.json -d your_config.json
# or
check-jsonschema --schemafile input_schema.json your_config.json
@end example

@subheading Root structure

@example
@{
  "version":          "3.0.0",
  "system":           @{ @dots{} @},
  "speakers":         @{ @dots{} @},
  "crossovers":       @{ @dots{} @},
  "target_curve":     "@dots{}",
  "optimizer":        @{ @dots{} @},
  "recording_config": @{ @dots{} @},
  "ctc":              @{ @dots{} @}
@}
@end example

@multitable @columnfractions .20 .12 .12 .56
@headitem Field @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{version} @tab string @tab no @tab Config version
  (semver). Default @code{"3.0.0"}.
@item @code{system} @tab object @tab no @tab Topology and logical
  channel mapping.
@item @code{speakers} @tab object @tab @strong{yes} @tab Map of
  channel names to speaker configurations.
@item @code{crossovers} @tab object @tab no @tab Named crossover
  filter blocks.
@item @code{target_curve} @tab string @tab no @tab Target frequency
  response curve.
@item @code{optimizer} @tab object @tab no @tab Optimisation
  parameters.
@item @code{recording_config} @tab object @tab no @tab Capture
  device / signal config.
@item @code{ctc} @tab object @tab no @tab Cross-talk cancellation /
  binaural correction using measured two-ear IRs or HRTF/SOFA data.
@end multitable

@subheading System block

@table @code
@item model
@code{stereo}, @code{home_cinema} or @code{custom}.
@item speakers
Map from logical role (@code{L}, @code{R}, @code{C}, @code{LS},
@code{RS}, @code{LB}, @code{RB}, @code{LFE}, @dots{}) to a speaker
key.
@item subwoofers
@code{config}: @code{single}, @code{multi}, @code{dba} or
@code{cardioid}; @code{crossover}: name of a crossover block;
@code{sub_meas}: routing.
@end table

@subheading Speakers block

A speaker entry is one of:

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Measurement reference} -- path to a CSV
  (@code{freq,spl[,phase]}) or a stringified speaker key.
@item @strong{Single speaker} -- inline measurement + optional
  smoothing.
@item @strong{Multi-driver Group} -- multiple drivers + their own
  crossovers.
@item @strong{MultiSub} -- multiple subs treated as a virtual channel
  (legacy gain/delay, or full multi-seat when paired with
  @code{optimizer.multi_seat}).
@item @strong{DBA} -- Double Bass Array (front wall + delayed back
  wall).
@item @strong{Cardioid} -- gradient cardioid pair for sidewall
  cancellation.
@end itemize

@subheading Crossovers

@example
"crossovers": @{
  "bass_xo": @{ "type": "LR24", "frequency": 80.0 @}
@}
@end example

Types: @code{LR24}, @code{LR48}, @code{BW12}, @code{BW24}.

@subheading Optimizer block

The optimiser block is large; the most useful keys are:

@table @code
@item num_filters
Number of IIR filters per channel.
@item algorithm
Optimiser back-end (e.g.@: @code{autoeq:de}, @code{autoeq:cobyla}).
@item max_iter
Evaluation budget.
@item min_freq, max_freq
Filter placement bounds in Hz.
@item min_q, max_q
Q bounds.
@item min_db, max_db
Per-filter gain bounds.
@item loss_type
@code{flat}, @code{score}, @code{epa}, @dots{} (@pxref{autoeq User
Guide}).
@item peq_model
Filter-set structure (@code{pk}, @code{pk+shelf}, @dots{}).
@item smoothness_penalty
TV^2 curvature regularisation
(@code{tv2_weight}, @code{schroeder_hz}, @code{modal_weight_scale},
@code{exponent}).
@item schroeder_split
Modal-vs-statistical split toggle.
@item excursion_protection
F3 detection + HPF generation.
@item phase_alignment
Sub-vs-main delay/polarity grid.
@item multi_seat
Multi-seat / SFM / modal-basis controls.
@item cea2034_correction
3-pass speaker pre-correction using on-axis / LW / SP curves.
@item processing_mode
@code{IIR}, @code{PhaseLinear}, @code{Hybrid}, @code{MixedPhase},
@code{LowLatency}.
@item fir
@code{taps}, @code{window}, @code{minimum_phase} settings.
@item group_delay
GD-Opt v2 controls (delay / polarity / all-pass or FIR shift).
@end table

@subheading CTC block

The optional @code{ctc} block exports a
@file{recommended_xtc_matrix.json} artefact loadable by the XTC
plugin with @code{source_mode: "roomeq_recommended"}. Supports
measured two-ear IRs (one stereo WAV per speaker x head position) or
HRTF/SOFA data, with a configurable window, regularisation
(@code{beta_db}, @code{beta_lf_db}, @code{beta_hf_db},
@code{max_gain_db}), robustness mode, and tap count.

@subheading Measurement CSV format

Two or three columns, header line optional:

@example
freq,spl[,phase]
20.0,-3.2[,0.0]
@dots{}
@end example

Frequency in Hz, SPL in dB, phase (optional) in radians or degrees as
indicated by header.

@c =====================================================================
@node RoomEQ DSP Chain Schema
@section RoomEQ Output Format
@cindex roomeq output format

The complete schema lives in
@file{crates/autoeq/bin/roomeq/output_schema.json} and is documented
in @file{OUTPUT_FORMAT.md}.

@subheading Root structure

@example
@{
  "version":  "1.4.0",
  "channels": @{ @dots{} @},
  "metadata": @{ @dots{} @}
@}
@end example

@subheading Channel DSP chain

Each channel has an ordered list of plugins that processes audio in
sequence, plus optional pre/post curves and IRs:

@example
"left": @{
  "channel":      "left",
  "plugins":      [ @dots{} ],
  "drivers":      [ @dots{} ],     // per-driver chains for multi-way speakers
  "initial_curve":           @{ @dots{} @},
  "final_curve":             @{ @dots{} @},
  "eq_response":             @{ @dots{} @},
  "target_curve":            @{ @dots{} @},
  "pre_ir":                  @{ @dots{} @},
  "post_ir":                 @{ @dots{} @},
  "fir_temporal_masking":    @{ @dots{} @}
@}
@end example

@subheading Plugin types

The output may contain any of these plugin entries, in chain order
(typically @code{gain -> delay -> eq -> convolution}):

@table @code
@item gain
Scalar dB gain.
@item eq
List of IIR biquads (@code{type}, @code{frequency}, @code{q},
@code{gain_db}).
@item crossover
@code{type} (@code{LR24} / @code{LR48} / @code{BW12} / @code{BW24}),
@code{frequency}.
@item delay
Time delay (samples or ms).
@item convolution
WAV file with FIR coefficients.
@item band_split
Split into bands by crossover frequencies.
@item band_merge
Sum bands back together.
@end table

@subheading Global plugins and routing

When bass management is active, @code{global_plugins} holds a sparse
matrix @code{crossover} plugin that the audio engine renders as a
routing stage before any per-channel plugins.

