@subheading Key public API

@table @code
@item autoeq::optim::optimize_filters
Generic optimiser entry point.
@item autoeq::optim::optimize_multi_driver
Multi-driver crossover optimiser.
@item autoeq::roomeq::optimize::optimize_room
Top-level RoomEQ entry point.
@item autoeq::roomeq::optimize::optimize_room_with_probe_arrivals
RoomEQ entry that skips WAV-onset detection and uses caller-supplied
per-channel arrival times.
@item autoeq::roomeq::workflows::*
Specialised topology workflows (stereo 2.0, stereo 2.1, home cinema).
@end table

@subheading Conventions

@itemize @bullet
@item Filters must be placed @strong{within} the measurement frequency
  bounds. The validator refuses configurations that violate this.
@item Passband detection uses @emph{relative-to-peak} thresholds, not
  absolute dB values.
@item The core filter type is @code{autoeq_iir::Biquad}; @code{Peak},
  @code{Lowshelf}, @code{Highshelf}, @code{Lowpass}, @code{Highpass},
  @code{Bandpass} and @code{Notch} are supported.
@item Optimiser backend names are looked up in
  @code{src/optim/registry.rs}; the @code{nlopt:*} aliases are
  deprecated but accepted.
@end itemize

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test  -p autoeq --lib
cargo check -p autoeq
cargo clippy -p autoeq --no-deps
just qa-roomeq
just qa-roomeq-convergence
@end example

The QA benchmark suite measures convergence and preference score over
a fixed corpus; regressions should not be merged.

